    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode de-duplication in `AssignCustomerCode.java` (the `customerCode` step of the `POST /api/owners` pipeline).\n\n**What changed:** `AssignCustomerCode.service(...)` now also injects `OwnerRepository`. After computing the base code (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`), it checks whether any existing owner already uses that `customerCode`. If so, it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n` \u2265 2 that produces a code no existing owner holds, then sets that de-duplicated value.\n\n**Why this fits the pipeline:** `AssignCustomerCode` runs before `SaveOwner`, so `findAll()` returns only already-persisted owners \u2014 the new owner isn't in the set yet, so the base code is kept when there's no genuine collision. Governance (`govern: [ transaction ]`) already spans the step, so the read participates in the request's transaction.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` (asserting distinct owners get distinct customer codes) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne note: the spec's exact-collision path (identical `normalizedTelephone + lastName`) can't be exercised black-box because telephone uniqueness (`RequireUniqueIdentity`) blocks it upstream \u2014 the test comment calls this out and asserts the guarantee (uniqueness) rather than forcing a hash collision.",
